@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+---
+name: live-context
+description: Pin, track and recall exact context sources while Context Language Models (the editable LIVE_CONTEXT.md mirror) is on in this session. Use before cutting a source from the mirror that later work must keep or find again. Every call fails with "Context Language Models are off in this session" otherwise.
+---
+
+# live-context
+
+```python
+import live_context
+
+# source: a CTX_TURN id from LIVE_CONTEXT.md or a session entry id
+r = await live_context.annotate("3-1a2b3c4d5e6f", "Deploy rule", "the user set it", "check before deploy", "pin")
+await live_context.list()                 # {"text": ..., "annotations": [...]}
+await live_context.recall(r["id"])        # {"text": exact source, "truncated": bool}
+await live_context.resolve(r["id"], "deployed")
+```
+
+Retention:
+- `pin` keeps the exact text visible in every request. Sources over 8000 tokens are refused.
+- `continuity` keeps a title, next action and recall id visible.
+- `archive` shows nothing; use `recall` to read it.
+
+`recall(id, max_tokens=2000)` returns at most `max_tokens` (128 to 8000) and fails if the source entry changed.
